                  testID="note-text-day-tithi-nakshatra"
                >
                  Shukla Ekadashi is a Nanda-class tithi and the fasting day of the bright fortnight; the tradition reads it for restraint, devotion and work that asks for a clear mind.
                   
                  The Moon is in Shatabhisha today, a movable (Chara) nakshatra ruled by Rahu and inside Panchak: read as good for study, the care of others and solitary work, with the Panchak customs observed.
                   
                  Thursday is Jupiter's day, read as favourable for learning, teachers, ceremonies, children and matters of faith and finance.
                   
                  Bhadra is on earth today from 
                  <Text
                    style={
                      [
                        {
                          "fontFamily": "NotoSans",
